# Auth and registry settings ONLY.
#
# Modern pnpm reads nothing else from this file: since pnpm 10 every other
# setting must live in `pnpm-workspace.yaml` (or the global config), and a
# setting placed here is ignored in silence rather than reported. That is how
# `link-workspace-packages` stopped taking effect during the pnpm 12 migration
# — it lived here, and moved to `linkWorkspacePackages` in
# `pnpm-workspace.yaml`. Put workspace settings there; leave this file for the
# registry and the credentials to reach it.
#
# npm still reads this file in full, which is the other reason to keep it thin:
# `create-nextly-app` scaffolds npm projects, and the smoke legs install with npm.

# Registry configuration (use npm public registry)
registry = https://registry.npmjs.org/

# Publishing auth: npm Trusted Publishing (OIDC). The release workflow
# exchanges its GitHub OIDC token at publish time, so no _authToken is
# stored here. Local publishes (not supported) would require `npm login`.
@nextlyhq:registry=https://registry.npmjs.org
